{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/268690-adventure-non-human-pc-s","id":268690,"title":"Adventure! Non-human PC's","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-29T19:06:53-07:00","id":268690,"title":"Adventure! Non-human PC's","content":"I'm going to be running a game of Adventure! in the near future that's based on pulp novels and cartoons, ignoring most of the setting metaplot and the tie-ins to Aberrant and Trinity. So for me, there's no need of Z-Waves or an eventual evolution into the other two settings. As part of that, I'm testing out the inclusion of active magic, even a Mystic Inspiration that uses Knacks modified over from the Thaumaturgical Merits in WOD: Second Sight.<br /> <br /> Taking my cue more from Dr. McNinja, Hellboy, Girl Genius and Thundar, I'm allowing non-human PC's. Types of characters like Judy the Gorilla, Gorilla Grodd, Ookla the Mok, Abe Sapien, and Dr. Johann Krauss. So far the only player to take me up on that potential is considering being a talking gorilla that hunts dinosaurs in the heart of Africa. None of the players have settled on their concept, but that's one of the ones he's considering.<br /> <br /> Currently, there won't be any mechanical benefits to being a talking gorilla, although I am considering something to offset the social penalties of being a talking gorilla. Maybe a higher limit on his Strength and Stamina than human would have. Similarly, if someone wanted to play a fishman like Abe Sapien, I might give them waterbreathing for free, or at least an increased ability to hold their breath and maneuver underwater. <br /> <br /> Has anyone else ever done something similar, or have any thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T06:47:49-07:00","id":268982,"title":"","content":"wasnt there even a inspired gorilla in the original (enkidu i belive)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/24.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/619-deadguy","name":"DeadGuy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:41:51-07:00","id":269313,"title":"","content":"Indeed there was, and he was a playable character in the demo adventure - sadly never published, so we don't have his stats handy, but as it was a demo I would guess he was made within normal Inspired stat ranges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T12:12:08-07:00","id":269325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/268690-adventure-non-human-pc-s?p=269313#post269313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed there was, and he was a playable character in the demo adventure - sadly never published, so we don't have his stats handy, but as it was a demo I would guess he was made within normal Inspired stat ranges.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's what Bruce Baugh told me, at least. He was done up as a stalwart to help account for his increased gorilla strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T16:29:43-07:00","id":270477,"title":"","content":"There's also, possibly, a <i>macaca mulatta novus</i> named Grandfather Monkey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:10:45-07:00","id":270959,"title":"","content":"Ive got 7 different alien species in my adventure! game. Each of them has a positive and negative trait. The lizard folk cant become inspired, and have access to a few knacks as racial traits that ise willpower instead. They are big and powerful, but slow and dimwitted (adding dots to str and stam and losing the auto dot to dex and wits) and have natural armor (super medical either sub dermal plating or the tough skin one) but are susceptible to cold damage. (Armor doesnt apply) their species descend from a dinosaur like race, who had brains like walnuts. They are a space faring race only because of a 65 million year head start over humans. Other species are done in similar ways-just depends on the creature they are based off of. Bird folk arent tough, but quick and can glide. Rat folk have enhanced smell, and boosts to stealth. But tho only species who as a whole, can be inspired, are humans, due to our ingenuity and ability to adapt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T11:14:53-07:00","id":270961,"title":"","content":"Basically, for humans, in the future, 1/1000 is inspired, even if its only 1 knack...I know thats rule bending what an inspired is, but I use the &quot;500 years worth of almost forced evolution&quot; reason. The other species used have odds starting in the millions with the bird folk, and rising sharply into the &quot;handful&quot; or even &quot;the only inpsired of their kind&quot; numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=392\" data-tempid=\"temp_392_1519878565794_106\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3676-manbearpig","name":"ManBearPig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}